.TH XG2G 1 "2026-07-30" "xg2g" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
xg2g \- serve Enigma2 live TV and recordings as browser-ready HLS
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B xg2g
.RB [ \-\-config
.IR path ]
.RB [ \-\-version ]
.br
.B xg2g
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B xg2g
is a Linux server daemon that connects to an Enigma2/OpenWebIF receiver,
selects direct-play, remux, or transcode paths, and exposes a WebUI and a
versioned HTTP API.
.PP
The supported persistent installation runs the daemon in a hardened container
managed by Docker Compose and systemd. Running
.B xg2g
without a command starts the daemon.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B config
Validate, dump, or migrate configuration files.
.TP
.B entitlements
Inspect and manage commercial unlock overrides.
.TP
.B storage
Verify SQLite storage and inspect decision history.
.TP
.B preflight
Run lifecycle checks against the effective configuration.
.TP
.B healthcheck
Probe daemon readiness or liveness.
.TP
.B diagnostic
Trigger an authenticated diagnostic action.
.TP
.B status
Show verified daemon status through the authenticated API.
.TP
.B report
Generate a redacted JSON evidence bundle.
.TP
.B help
Show help for a command.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-config " path"
Load the YAML configuration at
.IR path .
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print release, commit, and build metadata, then exit.
.TP
.B \-h
.TQ
.B \-\-help
Show command-specific help where supported.
.SH EXAMPLES
Validate a configuration:
.PP
.nf
xg2g config validate -f /etc/xg2g/config.yaml
.fi
.PP
Probe readiness:
.PP
.nf
xg2g healthcheck --mode=ready --port=8088
.fi
.PP
Show authenticated status:
.PP
.nf
xg2g status --token "$XG2G_API_TOKEN"
.fi
.PP
Write a redacted support report:
.PP
.nf
xg2g report --token "$XG2G_API_TOKEN" --out xg2g-report.json
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/xg2g/xg2g.env
Root-owned service environment and secrets.
.TP
.I /etc/xg2g/config.yaml
Optional system-wide YAML configuration.
.TP
.I /var/lib/xg2g
Persistent runtime state.
.TP
.I /srv/xg2g
Installed Compose, lifecycle, and verification bundle.
.SH SECURITY
Non-loopback browser access requires HTTPS. Protect API tokens and signing
secrets, and keep
.I /etc/xg2g/xg2g.env
owned by root with mode 0600.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR docker (1),
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR xg2g-admin (8)
.PP
Project documentation:
.UR https://github.com/ManuGH/xg2g
https://github.com/ManuGH/xg2g
.UE
